From: shuios <dev@shuios.local>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: resolve FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR relative to the config file

Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake bakes in the *target* install path
(/usr/lib/cmake) at build time. Addons such as fcitx5-rime and
fcitx5-gtk then include
${FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR}/Fcitx5Utils/Fcitx5CompilerSettings.cmake,
which does not exist during a cross build where Fcitx5 lives in the
staging sysroot.

Derive the directory from the config file's own location instead. This
is correct for both native and cross builds.

---
diff -u a/src/lib/fcitx-utils/Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake.in b/src/lib/fcitx-utils/Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake.in
--- a/src/lib/fcitx-utils/Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake.in
+++ b/src/lib/fcitx-utils/Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake.in
@@ -4,7 +4,10 @@
 include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/Fcitx5Macros.cmake")
 
 set(FCITX_SYS_INSTALL_PREFIX "@FCITX_INSTALL_PREFIX@")
-set(FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR "@FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR@")
+get_filename_component(FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR
+    "${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/.." ABSOLUTE)
+# 交叉编译时上面的路径是目标机路径（/usr/lib/cmake），构建机看不到；
+# 按配置文件位置推回 cmake 目录，原生/交叉都正确。
 
 set(_default_FCITX_INSTALL_USE_FCITX_SYS_PATHS Off)
 if (NOT DEFINED FCITX_INSTALL_USE_FCITX_SYS_PATHS)
